Subject: [LANDED round 237 under Decisions 95/96] NEMO closed-bottom W mask plus live Kmm T divisor

Status: LANDED in round 237 under Decisions 95/96.  Apply the round-229
closed-bottom-W-mask member first, then this patch.  The historical round-236
measurement and disclosed ratchet result below are retained unchanged.  Given
NEMO's recorded stage-3 entry, the pair makes hmsku,
hmskv, and the live e3t(Kmm) divisor bit-exact and reduces the maximum LDF
RHS residual from 7.2621621143171395e-11 to
4.9526264855300654e-12 K/s (93.180231441314%).  The certified SMT-3 ladder
improves 30 of 50 aggregate rows and worsens four, but the cellwise two-ULP
ratchet is red (40 violations; maximum worsening 431802197.9165039 row-scale
ULP).  Production was restored.

Compiled source:
VORTEX_SMT3_VEC_R16_OMIP_L1_P3/BLD/ppsrc/nemo/traldf_iso.f90:243-259
forms the closed W masks; :306-310/:327-331 divides by e3t(Kmm).
stprk3_stg.f90:531-532 calls tra_ldf at stage 3 with the stage-2 output as
Kmm, so the divisor SSH is the materialized half-stage field, not the
once-per-step slope SSH.

